schema: "0.4"
id: sem-detail-ux-design
type: image
quality: high
product_targets:
  - semtext.dev
tags:
  - semtext
  - sem-detail
  - ux-design
  - reference

prompt:
  text: |
    UX design sheet for the SemText `<sem-detail>` element — one prose
    passage inside a `sem-details` container, shown in all three of its
    reading states — one example reading page per state, stacked vertically,
    rendered in the minimal-tech-light theme on a dark slate canvas
    (bg #0f172a, surface #1e293b, fg #e2e8f0, accent #60a5fa). Each page is
    a bordered passage card (12px radius, hairline #334155 border,
    16px inner padding) inside a browser-chrome frame, labeled with a small
    mono uppercase caption. The card holds ordinary prose text — the card
    itself is NEVER drawn as a button: no fill change, no outline, no
    pointer-art on the card; only inline chips inside the prose carry
    interactive looks.

    Page 1 — caption "PLAIN (default)". One passage card: "The OIDC token
    travels in the Authorization header." The word "Authorization" is a
    recall target rendered as emphasis: an accent-blue tint behind the text
    at 18% opacity (soft luminous wash), 4px rounded corners, a few pixels
    of horizontal padding, glyphs in the normal foreground color and
    completely legible. Nothing on this page is occluded.

    Page 2 — caption "QUIZ". The identical passage, but "Authorization" is
    an occluded chip: a solid slate block (#475569), rounded 4px, at least
    3ch wide, no visible glyphs — a self-check recall mask set inline in the
    sentence, the rest of the prose fully readable. Beside the sentence, a
    small secondary state shows the same card after reveal: the word reads
    as in page 1 (accent tint, fully legible), demonstrating the one-way
    per-item reveal.

    Page 3 — caption "TWO PASSAGES IN ONE CONTAINER". Two passage cards
    stacked with a 12px gap inside one quiet container region: the first
    reads "Access tokens expire after 15 minutes; the client mints a new
    one from the refresh grant." (tinted target "15 minutes"); the second
    reads "Refresh tokens never reach the browser — they live in the
    server-side session." (tinted target "never reach the browser"). Plain
    view: both targets emphasized and legible, both cards calm prose blocks
    of identical weight — each passage is one independent unit.

    Typography: clean system sans (Inter-like), 16px body, 1.6 line
    height, generous margins. No extra chrome, no buttons other than the
    caption labels.
  negative: >
    occluded or blurred text on page 1 or on page 3; black bars over prose;
    redaction-marker aesthetic on the tint states; whole cards drawn as
    clickable buttons (fills, shadows, outlines, pointer cursors rendered
    as graphics); neon glow; italic highlight text; more or fewer than the
    three labeled pages; light background; watermark; lorem ipsum.
  style: >
    Flat UI spec sheet, minimal-tech aesthetic, restrained single-accent
    palette, crisp 12px card radius, hairline #334155 borders, generous
    negative space. Looks like a panel from a design-system guide.

attachments:
  - path: /Users/keithbrings/Work/Space/Noizu/.tmp/semtext-docs-overhaul/snaps/sem-detail/sem-detail-primary-render-1280.png
    role: reference
  - path: /Users/keithbrings/Work/Space/Noizu/.tmp/semtext-docs-overhaul/snaps/sem-detail/sem-detail-quiz-render-1280.png
    role: reference
  - path: /Users/keithbrings/Work/Space/Noizu/.tmp/semtext-docs-overhaul/snaps/sem-detail/sem-detail-quiz-render-reveal-1280.png
    role: reference
  - path: /Users/keithbrings/Work/Space/Noizu/.tmp/semtext-docs-overhaul/snaps/sem-detail/sem-detail-multi-passage-render-1280.png
    role: reference

output:
  dimensions:
    width: 1280
    height: 1280
    aspect_ratio: "1:1"
  formats:
    - format: png
      filename: sem-detail-ux-design.png

requirements:
  modes:
    - id: plain
      label: "PLAIN (default)"
      must_show:
        - one bordered prose passage card with the full sentence readable
        - the recall target as an accent-blue tint behind the text at
          reduced opacity (18%), 4px rounded, horizontal padding
        - tinted glyphs in the normal foreground color, full contrast
      must_never:
        - occlude, blur, bar or mask the target on this page
        - present the passage card itself as a button or link
    - id: quiz
      label: "QUIZ"
      must_show:
        - the same passage with the target replaced by a solid slate
          occlusion chip (#475569), rounded, min 3ch wide, no glyphs
        - the surrounding prose fully readable next to the chip
        - "a revealed state shown beside it: accent-tinted, fully legible
          word, demonstrating the one-way per-item reveal"
      must_never:
        - keep the occlusion on the plain or two-passage pages
        - reveal more than the demonstrated item at once
        - use transparency or partial legibility for the occluded chip
    - id: multi-passage
      label: "TWO PASSAGES IN ONE CONTAINER"
      must_show:
        - two equal-weight passage cards as siblings in one container
        - each card with its own emphasized, fully legible target
        - calm 12px gap between the cards; no nesting boxes
      must_never:
        - merge the two passages into one card
        - draw the second card differently (size, border, tint) from the first

eval:
  pass_threshold: 0.75
  criteria:
    passage-is-prose:
      weight: 0.35
      description: >
        Every passage card reads as prose content, not as an interactive
        control: border + surface + padding only, on all three pages.
      fail_signals:
        - button fills, strong shadows or outlines on cards
        - pointer/affordance art on the card itself
    target-states:
      weight: 0.35
      description: >
        Plain and two-passage pages show targets as 18% accent tint with
        fully legible glyphs; the quiz page shows one solid slate chip plus
        its revealed counterpart.
      fail_signals:
        - occluded text anywhere on page 1 or page 3
        - chip on the quiz page shows ghosted or partially readable glyphs
        - revealed state missing
    card-structure:
      weight: 0.2
      description: >
        Page 3 shows two independent, equal passage cards with their own
        targets inside one quiet container.
      fail_signals:
        - a single merged card
        - unequal cards (different borders, tints or sizes)
    theme-fidelity:
      weight: 0.1
      description: >
        Dark minimal-tech palette (#0f172a bg, #60a5fa accent), hairline
        borders, mono uppercase captions, exactly three labeled pages.
      fail_signals:
        - light background or multiple accent hues
        - more or fewer than three labeled pages
  reject_if:
    - any page occludes or hides body prose outside a quiz chip
    - a passage card is drawn as a clickable button across its whole area
    - any page shows illegible body copy
